5.8,48.7 216.7,61.1 241.5,79.2 243.8,80.0 224.2,78.7 197.8,66.2 189.4,49.7 196.2,36.8 223.2,35.6 248.2,50.2 249.5,63.4 226.4,69.3 201.3,67.5 184.4,56.7 196.1,51.3 222.5,51.4 237.0,52.5 223.4,57.4 200.4,55.5 185.3,53.0 190.0,50.8 210.8,53.1 223.5,43.0 212.0,24.8 187.3,24.6 199.4,52.8 224.3,79.9 232.1,92.3 211.6,79.8 186.2,55.7 177.6,40.3 196.0,45.4 223.1,56.6 228.5,62.1 202.8,63.7 183.6,58.9 201.9,52.3 233.4,56.8 227.4,54.9 202.0,54.3 190.0,47.3 180.0,47.0 192.0,81.7 209.3,109.4 215.4,103.7 209.0,62.1 200.8,36.3 195.1,35.8 208.5,62.6 237.0,96.2 244.1,78.9 201.5,62.4 223.7,69.0 235.4,63.2 203.8,70.4 171.9,61.3 206.0,69.1 234.4,79.2 237.1,78.3 189.3,69.6 196.1,55.6 225.3,57.7 243.9,63.5 225.7,75.4 189.8,73.4 192.7,69.9 220.4,65.0 228.2,61.5 202.2,69.1 180.8,65.5 192.5,58.6 228.3,54.7 235.4,54.6 218.2,58.3 203.2,59.1 230.0,81.0 229.5,71.8 202.1,52.8 184.7,40.2 207.1,64.9 225.8,74.7 184.2,52.9 186.8,43.0 216.9,54.0 210.5,74.7 185.1,59.4 207.0,55.9 206.3,61.6 194.2,59.2 191.7,57.4 209.0,70.1 222.1,71.0 195.5,61.3 177.7,53.4 178.8,61.1 206.0,71.6 220.7,70.4\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg><span>Explore in 3D (about 4 MB)</span></button><div class=\"mvv\" data-mvv=\"scene\" data-mode=\"site\" data-src=\"/media/examples/virig-5imus-4cams/views0.json\"></div></div>", "result": "<p>The solved positions and orientations, to scale in the IMU frame. Drag sideways to orbit. Tap a sensor to see its values.</p><div class=map><div class=stage><canvas id=rig tabindex=0 aria-label=\"3D map of the cameras and IMU\"></canvas><div class=tools><button data-view=iso type=button>3D</button><button data-view=front type=button>Front</button><button data-view=top type=button>Top</button><button data-view=side type=button>Side</button><button data-z=1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button><button data-z=-1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button></div></div><div class=panel><div class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></div></div></div><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Sensor</th><th>fx, fy, cx, cy px</th><th>Lever mm</th><th>log(R) rad</th><th>td ms</th><th>t_ga ms</th><th>Reprojection px</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>cam0</th><td>286.4, 285.6, 415.1, 404.4</td><td>[−158.3, −108.7, −26.5]</td><td>[+1.5620, −0.0073, −0.0249]</td><td>−0.19</td><td></td><td>0.188</td></tr><tr><th>cam1</th><td>286.5, 285.4, 414.0, 398.8</td><td>[−94.8, −109.5, −27.8]</td><td>[+1.5646, −0.0044, −0.0205]</td><td>−0.15</td><td></td><td>0.192</td></tr><tr><th>cam2</th><td>286.2, 285.1, 416.3, 401.1</td><td>[−160.5, −110.4, −49.8]</td><td>[+1.5664, +0.0216, −0.0566]</td><td>−0.30</td><td></td><td>0.204</td></tr><tr><th>cam3</th><td>286.5, 285.5, 412.7, 399.8</td><td>[−97.2, −111.1, −53.2]</td><td>[+1.5732, +0.0216, −0.0512]</td><td>−0.27</td><td></td><td>0.215</td></tr><tr><th>IMU (base)</th><td></td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>−0.56 ± 0.17</td><td></td></tr><tr><th>IMU gx3_25</th><td></td><td>[−122.0, −46.9, −2.9]</td><td>[−2.2372, −2.1947, +0.0186]</td><td>−0.43</td><td>+0.12 ± 0.20</td><td></td></tr><tr><th>IMU gx3_35</th><td></td><td>[−82.3, −47.4, −3.4]</td><td>[−2.2388, −2.1989, +0.0128]</td><td>−2.01</td><td>+0.01 ± 0.21</td><td></td></tr><tr><th>IMU t265_01</th><td></td><td>[−145.8, −104.2, −25.9]</td><td>[−0.0085, −2.1884, +2.1962]</td><td>−7.03</td><td>−6.58 ± 0.18</td><td></td></tr><tr><th>IMU t265_03</th><td></td><td>[−148.2, −105.5, −51.0]</td><td>[+0.0221, −2.1744, +2.1712]</td><td>−7.12</td><td>−6.59 ± 0.17</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Lever arms and rotations are each sensor in the base IMU frame; rotation is log(R) in rad. td is the time offset to the base IMU, t_imu = t_sensor + td. Reprojection is the median per camera (all cameras: median 0.196 px): how well the model fits the corners, not how accurate it is.</p>", "check": "<div class=ex-callout><p><b>No published reference.</b> No published calibration exists for this rig, so this page has nothing to compare against. What we can show is how much each value moves from one recording to the next. <a href=\"/benchmark/results/virig-5imus-4cams/\">All 7 recordings: Dataset eval →</a></p></div>", "config": "<p>The marked lines are the choices that matter for this rig:</p><ul class=list><li><code>input.imu_topics</code>: Five IMU topics. The first is the base IMU; the other four are solved against it.</li><li><code>input.window_mode</code>: MVIS picks the 80 s window with the most motion; this recording is shorter, so all of it is used.</li><li><code>camera_input.cameras</code>: The three cameras after the first are added to the graph at 4 Hz, which keeps the solve small.</li><li><code>camera_input.path</code>: The starting camera intrinsics, from camera-only solves of all 7 recordings.</li><li><code>solve.estimate_t_ga</code>: Estimates t_ga, the time offset between the gyroscope and the accelerometer. The T265 IMUs need it most.</li><li><code>estimate.board_points</code>: The printed board is not quite flat, so its shape is estimated too.</li><li><code>estimate.camera.intrinsics</code>: Camera intrinsics stay free in the camera + IMU solve.</li></ul><p class=note>This is the config of the run on this page, with every path cut to its file name. Point the paths at your copy.</p><p>The solve took about 7 min on one desktop. It writes <code>cam_imu.json</code>, a calibration YAML and a report beside the config.</p><dl class=ex-kv><dt>MVIS</dt><dd>MVIS main, 2026-11-10</dd><dt>Run date</dt><dd>2026-11-10</dd><dt>Data</dt><dd><a href=\"/datasets/virig-5imus-4cams/\">VI-Rig 5 IMUs + 4 cams dataset page →</a></dd><dt>Config</dt><dd><code>virig_5imus_4cams_cam_imu.yaml</code>, above</dd><dt>Command</dt><dd><code>mvis cam-imu -c virig_5imus_4cams_cam_imu.yaml</code></dd></dl>", "dataset": "<div class=two><div><ul class=list><li>Recording 5imus_4cams_01, one of the 7 recordings of this rig. It is about 59 s long, shorter than the 80 s window MVIS asks for, so the whole recording is used.</li><li>Cameras: the fisheye pairs of two T265 units, all global shutter, with the equidistant lens model. Each pair is synced inside its unit, but the two units are not synced to each other; their time offsets are solved against the base IMU.</li><li>IMUs: the Xsens MTi is the base IMU; the two MicroStrain units and the two T265 IMUs are solved against it.</li><li>Board: AprilGrid 6×6, tag 88 mm, spacing 0.3, t36h11.</li><li>Solve window: 58.7 s.</li></ul><p>Download: <a href=\"/datasets/virig-5imus-4cams/\">VI-Rig 5 IMUs + 4 cams dataset page →</a> The recordings are listed there, not copied here.</p></div><div><figure class=board><svg viewBox=\"-52.8 -52.8 765.6 765.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"AprilGrid 6 by 6, to scale\"><rect x=\"-52.8\" y=\"-52.8\" width=\"765.6\" height=\"765.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path fill=\"#111\" d=\"M-26.40 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 -26.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 88.00h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 202.40h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 316.80h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM-26.40 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM88.00 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM202.40 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM316.80 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM431.20 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM545.60 431.20h26.40v26.40h-26.40zM660.00 431.20h26.4